00:48:15,400 --> 00:48:17,360
哎呀，疼！
Oh, ow!

764
00:48:20,480 --> 00:48:22,200
开始了！
Here we go!

765
00:48:26,320 --> 00:48:29,710
我没跟他说
我背不好。哎呀！
I didn't tell him
I had a bad back. Aya!

766
00:48:29,760 --> 00:48:32,560
詹姆斯被轻轻放在岸边…
'James was deposited
gently on the bank...'

767
00:48:34,160 --> 00:48:35,910
哎呀。
Ow.

768
00:48:35,960 --> 00:48:39,230
好嘞，行吧，
我们俩已经在…
Okey-doke, right, good,
we're both in...

769
00:48:39,280 --> 00:48:41,550
肯定是阿根廷了。
definitely Argentina now.

770
00:48:41,600 --> 00:48:45,430
然后我们被一阵熟悉的声音打断了。
'And then we were interrupted
by a familiar sound.'

771
00:48:45,480 --> 00:48:48,520
远处的汽车发动机声
CAR ENGINE IN DISTANCE

772
00:48:51,600 --> 00:48:52,950
那是……？
Is that...?

773
00:48:53,000 --> 00:48:54,600
不可能吧。
It can't be.

774
00:49:00,440 --> 00:49:02,640
别想这么轻松把我甩掉，伙计们。
Not going to lose me
that easily, boys.

775
00:49:04,360 --> 00:49:05,840
那是野马。
That is the Mustang.

776
00:49:07,160 --> 00:49:09,320
他到底怎么修好的？
How the hell's he mended that?

777
00:49:10,320 --> 00:49:15,080
不幸的是，哈蒙德随后
毁掉了他登场的壮丽。
'Unfortunately, Hammond then rather
spoiled the majesty of his arrival.'

778
00:49:20,680 --> 00:49:22,630
他卡住了。
He's stuck.

779
00:49:22,680 --> 00:49:24,630
我卡住了。
I'm stuck.

780
00:49:24,680 --> 00:49:26,880
杰里米笑了
JEREMY LAUGHS

781
00:49:28,280 --> 00:49:31,070
杰里米，詹姆斯，
那是你们吗？
Jeremy and James,
is that you over there?

782
00:49:31,120 --> 00:49:32,590
确实是。
It certainly is.

783
00:49:32,640 --> 00:49:35,230
好吧，你跨过河，
就到阿根廷了。
Well, you come over the river
and then you're in Argentina.

784
00:49:35,280 --> 00:49:36,590
哎呀！
Oo-ee!

785
00:49:36,640 --> 00:49:40,270
好啊，是的，嘿，嗯，
但我怎么过去河啊？
Well, yeah, hello, yeah,
but how do I come over the river?

786
00:49:40,320 --> 00:49:43,110
开车过去。这是个涉水点。
You drive over it. It's a ford.

787
00:49:43,160 --> 00:49:46,520
~ 这根本不是浅滩，是河。
~ 我们开过去了。轻而易举。
~ It's not a ford, it's a river.
~ We drove over. Easy.

788
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:50,750
可惜的是，因为哈蒙德
陷进泥里，
'Sadly, because Hammond
was bogged down,

789
00:49:50,800 --> 00:49:54,590
我们只好请当地的
挖掘机司机去把他拉出来。
'we had to ask a local
digger driver to go and get him.'

790
00:49:54,640 --> 00:49:59,550
好吧，你能先‘呲呲’
过去然后拖走吗？
OK, could you "chuga-chuga"
over and then tow?

791
00:49:59,600 --> 00:50:01,590
~ 司机说西班牙语
~ 嗯？
~ DRIVER SPEAKS SPANISH
~ Eh?

792
00:50:01,640 --> 00:50:04,320
~ 司机说西班牙语
~ 好的。
~ DRIVER SPEAKS SPANISH
~ Yes.

793
00:50:05,640 --> 00:50:09,840
多亏我那精彩的哑剧，
那位好心人很快就走了。
'Thanks to my brilliant miming, the
kindly chap was soon on his way.'

794
00:50:11,960 --> 00:50:13,870
我的意思是，哈蒙德
觉得我们是开车横穿过去的。
I mean, Hammond thinks
we drove across it.

795
00:50:13,920 --> 00:50:16,560
等会儿他会
大吃一惊。
He's in for quite
a surprise in a minute.

796
00:50:18,680 --> 00:50:23,560
嗯，这突然看起来
不太妙。噢。
Yeah, this is suddenly seeming
like not such a good idea. Oh.

797
00:50:27,320 --> 00:50:29,710
哎呀，好深啊。
Oh, it's deep.

798
00:50:29,760 --> 00:50:32,880
那是车门底部吗？
对，就是车门底部。
Is that the bottom of the doors?
Yeah, it's the bottom of the doors.

799
00:50:34,680 --> 00:50:37,080
水倒进来
哎呀，水进来了。
WATER POURING
Oh, there is water coming in.

800
00:50:38,120 --> 00:50:39,880
车里现在进了好多水。
Lot of water now in my car.

801
00:50:41,400 --> 00:50:42,790
要是他看到这辆货车的话……
If he sees this lorry...

802
00:50:42,840 --> 00:50:45,840
说实话，他可能会大发雷霆。我们可能得躲起来。
He might be really angry, actually.
We might have to hide.

803
00:50:48,840 --> 00:50:52,630
水从里面喷出来，量还挺大的。
There is water coming out,
quite a lot of it.

804
00:50:52,680 --> 00:50:54,630
它们在哪儿？
Where are they?

805
00:50:54,680 --> 00:50:56,830
应该看到詹姆斯要过河来了。
Should've seen James
coming across the river.

806
00:50:56,880 --> 00:50:59,550
水几乎淹到窗顶了，简直惊人。
It was almost up to the
top of the windows. Phenomenal.

807
00:50:59,600 --> 00:51:03,240
~ 是啊。~ 你把它们从河边开到这儿又弄得一团泥。
~ Yeah. ~ You got them quite muddy again
in the drive from the river to here.

808
00:51:09,520 --> 00:51:13,230
第二天，我们一大早上路，哈蒙德还担心
'The next day, we were on the road
early, with Hammond worrying about

809
00:51:13,280 --> 00:51:16,760
他在阿尔卑斯赛道的连杆端修补质量。
'the quality of his alpine
track rod end fix.

810
00:51:17,840 --> 00:51:20,320
希望这焊点别掉。
I hope that weld holds.

811
00:51:21,600 --> 00:51:24,750
要是掉了，这镜头就要翻车了。
If it doesn't, this shot is
going to get very tumbly.

812
00:51:24,800 --> 00:51:28,080
天空、地面、天空、地面、天空、地面，尖叫连连。
Sky, ground, sky, ground,
sky, ground, screaming.

813
00:51:29,360 --> 00:51:33,230
不过离乌斯怀亚只有几英里了，而且在那里，
'But there were only a few miles
to go to Ushuaia, and there,

814
00:51:33,280 --> 00:51:38,710
一支当地团队已经开始为我们的体育场打地基。
'a team of locals had already begun
the groundwork for our stadium.

815
00:51:38,760 --> 00:51:40,630
他们在用装运集装箱，
'They were using
shipping containers,

816
00:51:40,680 --> 00:51:44,110
这些将构成框架，而我们甚至已经排好
'which would form the framework,
and we had even lined up

817
00:51:44,160 --> 00:51:47,200
一些供阿根廷人使用的足球车。
'some football cars
for the Argentinians to use.'

818
00:51:49,280 --> 00:51:51,550
但随后我们收到消息，前面
But then we received word
that up ahead

819
00:51:51,600 --> 00:51:54,790
有人在抗议我们这次来访，
there was some kind of protest
about our visit,

820
00:51:54,840 --> 00:51:59,360
制作组决定我们最好搬到附近的酒店去。
and the producers decided it'd be
best if we went to a nearby hotel.

821
00:52:09,400 --> 00:52:12,630
停车场那帮是谁，詹姆斯？你认识吗？
Who's that lot in the car park,
James? Do you know?

822
00:52:12,680 --> 00:52:16,430
不认识，我见过，但不清楚他们是谁。
No. I've seen them before,
but I'm not sure who they are.

823
00:52:16,480 --> 00:52:21,430
这帮人对我们的摄像车很感兴趣。
Well, this lot are taking a lot
of interest in the camera vehicles.

824
00:52:21,480 --> 00:52:23,070
到底怎么回事？
What is it?

825
00:52:23,120 --> 00:52:26,680
我不知道这些家伙从哪儿冒出来的，但他们正朝这边走。
I don't know what these blokes came
out of but they're heading this way.

826
00:52:29,040 --> 00:52:30,670
他们从前面下来了。
They're coming down the front.

827
00:52:30,720 --> 00:52:32,630
是谁？他们要上来吗？
Who is? Are they coming up here?

828
00:52:32,680 --> 00:52:35,470
~ 哔——。~ 詹姆斯，请把脸收回去。
~ BLEEP. ~ James, please
keep your face back.

829
00:52:35,520 --> 00:52:38,470
你已经看到那辆挂着旗帜之类的车了。
You've seen the vehicle there with
the flag and all that kind of stuff.

830
00:52:38,520 --> 00:52:40,430
我们正要…大概有十来个
We were getting...
There must be about 10 or 15

831
00:52:40,480 --> 00:52:42,190
就在大堂里。
in the foyer just now.

832
00:52:42,240 --> 00:52:45,630
我已经和经理谈过了。他有点…
I've spoke to the manager.
He's a little bit...

833
00:52:45,680 --> 00:52:47,870
没办法…他也帮不上太多。
Nothing... Not a lot that he can do,

834
00:52:47,920 --> 00:52:51,470
所以我觉得现在，如果大家都待在各自的房间里…
so I think at the moment,
if we all stay in our rooms...

835
00:52:51,520 --> 00:52:54,160
好吧，情况是这样的。
All right. Here's the situation.

836
00:52:55,360 --> 00:52:58,150
我们被关在这间屋子里。我不知道这是谁的
We're holed up in this room.
I don't know whose it is

837
00:52:58,200 --> 00:53:00,270
但这不是我们的……
but it isn't ours...

838
00:53:00,320 --> 00:53:03,240
里面有一帮…
There's a gang...

839
00:53:04,520 --> 00:53:08,910
…民族主义者，之类的，觉得福克兰是阿根廷的，
.. nationalists, whatever, believe
that the Falklands are Argentinian,

840
00:53:08,960 --> 00:53:13,390
他们不喜欢英方，而他们就在酒店里。
they don't like the British,
and they're in the hotel.

841
00:53:13,440 --> 00:53:16,950
我们卡在这儿，根本不知道发生了啥。
And we're stuck in here
and we don't know what's going on.

842
00:53:17,000 --> 00:53:20,510
‘示威者里头有几位福克兰战争老兵’
'The protestors consisted of
some Falkland War veterans

843
00:53:20,560 --> 00:53:22,270
‘还有他们的同伙，’
'and their associates,

844
00:53:22,320 --> 00:53:26,070
‘他们说要是我们不停止拍摄，就要闹事了。’
'who said that if we didn't stop
filming, there would be trouble.

845
00:53:26,120 --> 00:53:31,510
‘警察一到现场，我们立马意识到这可不是空口白话。’
'The arrival of the police made us
realise this was no idle threat.'

846
00:53:31,560 --> 00:53:33,950
他会说西班牙语
HE SPEAKS SPANISH

847
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:36,910
这位老兵指责我们在保时捷上装了假车牌
The head veteran accused us
of putting a fake number plate

848
00:53:36,960 --> 00:53:37,990
在那辆保时捷上，
on the Porsche,

849
00:53:38,040 --> 00:53:41,790
那是故意挑衅福克兰战争的暗示。
that was a deliberate reference
to the Falklands War.

850
00:53:41,840 --> 00:53:45,310
我们的制片人解释说那车牌并非假的，而且
Our producers tried to explain
it wasn't fake and that it would be

851
00:53:45,360 --> 00:53:49,560
只是为了踢球的演练用，却毫无说服力。
replaced for the game of football,
but they got nowhere.

852
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:54,270
我们现在正跟警察开会呢。
We're in a meeting
with the police now.

853
00:53:54,320 --> 00:53:57,670
你是说我们得赶紧从火地岛滚蛋？
Are you saying we've got to get
the hell out of Tierra del Fuego?

854
00:53:57,720 --> 00:53:59,990
当然。
Absolutely.

855
00:54:00,040 --> 00:54:03,710
我们被要求离开火地岛，对吧？
We're being ordered to leave
Tierra del Fuego, yes?

856
00:54:03,760 --> 00:54:07,080
是的，他们想把我们这帮人赶走。
We are. They want us,
as people, out.

857
00:54:11,280 --> 00:54:14,630
我们刚被下令离开火地岛，
We have just been ordered out
of Tierra del Fuego,

858
00:54:14,680 --> 00:54:17,440
被赶出——实际上是——阿根廷。
ordered out of - effectively -
Argentina.

859
00:54:20,760 --> 00:54:23,910
可我们根本没有……我们一点怨气都没有
But we haven't... We haven't had
any animosity whatsoever

860
00:54:23,960 --> 00:54:28,990
整个旅程都如此。大家都很彬彬有礼，特别有魅力。
in the whole trip. Everybody's been
perfectly decent, very charming.

861
00:54:29,040 --> 00:54:32,470
我们来这儿只想踢场足球，
All we wanted to do was
come here and play football,

862
00:54:32,520 --> 00:54:34,960
结果却是……
and what's happened is...

863
00:54:40,320 --> 00:54:42,950
‘制片人说要花24小时
'The producers said
it would take 24 hours

864
00:54:43,000 --> 00:54:46,430
才能安排这么大一支剧组的撤离，
'to organise the departure
of such a large crew,

865
00:54:46,480 --> 00:54:48,430
可是即便警察在场，
'but even though
the police were present,

866
00:54:48,480 --> 00:54:51,230
老兵们说有一群暴徒正冲来
'the veterans said
a mob was on its way

867
00:54:51,280 --> 00:54:54,760
并警告说如果我们三分钟内不走，就会血腥冲突。
'and that there would be violence
if we weren't gone in three.'

868
00:54:57,600 --> 00:55:00,110
好啦，伙计们，快各自抓点装备。
Right, guys, everyone grab
a bit of equipment, please.

869
00:55:00,160 --> 00:55:02,400
大家都抓点东西，行不？
Everyone grab something, OK?

870
00:55:07,080 --> 00:55:08,800
我们能有护送吗？
Do we get an escort?

871
00:55:11,600 --> 00:55:14,270
‘与此同时，咱们三个人——他们的主要目标
'Meanwhile, the three of us,
who were the main target

872
00:55:14,320 --> 00:55:18,830
‘被抗议者怒火盯上，仍然躲在房间里。’
'for the protesters' anger,
were still holed up in our room.'

873
00:55:18,880 --> 00:55:21,750
现在，我们一路上干了不少布奇·卡西迪的事，
Now, we've been doing a whole load
of Butch Cassidy stuff on the way

874
00:55:21,800 --> 00:55:23,160
就在这儿，结果……
over here, and...

875
00:55:24,520 --> 00:55:28,350
~ 来吧。~ 这可是真正的布奇·卡西迪。
~ Come on.
~ This is Butch Cassidy for real.

876
00:55:28,400 --> 00:55:31,070
各位，上车吧。
Guys, everyone in the cars.

877
00:55:31,120 --> 00:55:34,350
车里装了四吨设备，
With four tonnes of equipment
loaded into the cars,

878
00:55:34,400 --> 00:55:38,400
31人的摄制组离开了小镇。
the 31-strong film crew
headed out of town.

879
00:55:44,000 --> 00:55:46,240
不久天色便暗了下来。
And soon darkness fell.

880
00:55:54,760 --> 00:55:57,910
警车护送得走184英里
A police escort would
take them 184 miles

881
00:55:57,960 --> 00:56:03,030
前往边境小镇圣塞巴斯蒂安，准备跨进智利，
to the border town of San Sebastian,
where they'd cross over into Chile,

882
00:56:03,080 --> 00:56:05,510
鉴于抗议者的诉求已经得到满足，
and since the protestors' demands
had been met,

883
00:56:05,560 --> 00:56:08,510
机组人员以为已经脱离危险。
the crew hoped
they were out of danger.

884
00:56:08,560 --> 00:56:12,400
但不久后，他们发现并不只有他们自己。
But a short while later,
they realised they were not alone.

885
00:56:13,400 --> 00:56:17,840
摩托车紧跟在明星座驾后面。摩托车紧跟在明星座驾后面。
Bikes behind the star cars.
Bikes behind the star cars.

886
00:56:21,240 --> 00:56:23,360
他们停下来，往里张望。
They're stopping and looking in.

887
00:56:25,320 --> 00:56:27,760
在找那辆保时捷。
They're looking for the Porsche.

888
00:56:37,840 --> 00:56:42,070
在唯一的道路上，荒郊野岭，连信号都没有，
On the only road, in the middle
of nowhere, with no phone signal,

889
00:56:42,120 --> 00:56:43,830
机组被追得团团转。
the crew were being hounded.

890
00:56:43,880 --> 00:56:46,230
车子嘟——
CAR BEEPS

891
00:56:46,280 --> 00:56:48,390
他们要开疯了。
They're going to be aggressive.

892
00:56:48,440 --> 00:56:51,070
随后，就在托洛温镇外，
Then, just outside
the town of Tolowin,

893
00:56:51,120 --> 00:56:55,600
警察命令车队停下，做好迎战准备。
the police told the convoy to
pull over and prepare for an attack.

894
00:57:10,080 --> 00:57:13,830
他们驶进镇子时，一大群人已经在等着。
As they drove into town,
a large mob was waiting.

895
00:57:13,880 --> 00:57:16,630
左边那帮人，真是人山人海。
The people on the left,
a lot of people on the left.

896
00:57:16,680 --> 00:57:18,390
~ 哔—— ~ 看这玩意儿。
~ BLEEP ~ hell, look at this.

897
00:57:18,440 --> 00:57:21,110
~ 是啊，这里人真多。~ 哔——。
~ Yeah, there's a lot of people here.
~ BLEEP.

898
00:57:21,160 --> 00:57:22,750
~ 哔——，~ 到处都是。
~ BLEEP, ~ they're everywhere.

899
00:57:22,800 --> 00:57:24,950
而且他们组织得严严实实。
And they were organised.

900
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:27,190
~ 还有辆卡车在拖慢我们。~ 哔——。
~ And there's a truck
slowing us down too. ~ BLEEP.

901
00:57:27,240 --> 00:57:29,790
那卡车占了右侧车道。
The truck blocking
the right-hand lane.

902
00:57:29,840 --> 00:57:33,390
~ 太慢了。这是故意的~ 哔——~ 卡车，就这么卡在这里。
~ It's too slow. That's a deliberate
~ BLEEP ~ truck, just put there.

903
00:57:33,440 --> 00:57:35,590
他们冲出来了。 他倒抽一口气
They're coming out.
HE GASPS

904
00:57:35,640 --> 00:57:36,830
哔——。
BLEEP.

905
00:57:36,880 --> 00:57:39,720
前几发是被鸡蛋打的。
The first couple of hits
were from eggs.

906
00:57:41,120 --> 00:57:44,030
随后石头也跟着来了。
But then the rocks started.

907
00:57:44,080 --> 00:57:45,990
甩石头，甩石头。
Throwing stones, throwing stones.

908
00:57:46,040 --> 00:57:49,110
各种东西往我们这儿砸。
Stuff lobbed at us.

909
00:57:49,160 --> 00:57:52,550
砰砰声
BANGING

910
00:57:52,600 --> 00:57:55,190
~ 哔—— ~ 开车！~ 哔——~ 开车！
~ BLEEP ~ drive, ~ BLEEP ~ drive!

911
00:57:55,240 --> 00:57:56,910
警笛尖叫
SIRENS WAIL

912
00:57:56,960 --> 00:58:00,150
你们没事吧？看看这帮子人。
You all right? Look at this lot.

913
00:58:00,200 --> 00:58:03,270
砰砰声和警笛
BANGING AND SIRENS

914
00:58:03,320 --> 00:58:05,390
哔——。
BLEEP.

915
00:58:05,440 --> 00:58:07,470
警笛
SIRENS

916
00:58:07,520 --> 00:58:10,200
男子大吼（西班牙语）
MAN SHOUTING IN SPANISH

917
00:58:16,000 --> 00:58:18,750
继续上，继续上。
Keep it going, keep it going.

918
00:58:18,800 --> 00:58:20,950
哔——。
BLEEP.

919
00:58:21,000 --> 00:58:23,720
砰砰声和警笛
BANGING AND SIRENS

920
00:58:25,040 --> 00:58:28,310
小心，小心右侧，小心右侧。
Look out, look out on your right,
look out on your right.

921
00:58:28,360 --> 00:58:31,310
往左，往左。  
继续，继续。
Go left, go left.
Keep going, keep going.

922
00:58:31,360 --> 00:58:34,030
现在往右猛踩油门，往右猛踩油门。
Now floor it to the right,
floor it to the right.

923
00:58:34,080 --> 00:58:35,790
砰——
BANGING

924
00:58:35,840 --> 00:58:37,480
继续前进。
Keep going.

925
00:58:39,360 --> 00:58:42,110
保持冷静。保持冷静。左边。
Keep calm. Keep calm. Left.

926
00:58:42,160 --> 00:58:44,520
让车队继续走。保持前进。
Keep the convoy rolling.
Keep it going.

927
00:58:46,840 --> 00:58:49,320
让卡尔……卡尔，往我们前面拐过去。
Keep Karl... Karl,
pull in in front of us.

928
00:58:53,640 --> 00:58:56,320
砰——
BANGING

929
00:59:06,320 --> 00:59:09,270
离开镇子后，车队里有两个人受伤，
Out of the town, the crew,
two of whom had been hurt,

930
00:59:09,320 --> 00:59:13,870
他们在路边停下来修理那一堆碎掉的窗户。
pulled over to repair
the multitude of smashed windows.

931
00:59:13,920 --> 00:59:16,750
好吧，我们现在来帮丹吧。
Right, let's help Dan
on this one now.

932
00:59:16,800 --> 00:59:19,190
而且他们就是麻烦的磁铁，
And because they were
a magnet for trouble,

933
00:59:19,240 --> 00:59:22,840
只好把保时捷、福特和莲花抛下。
they had to abandon
the Porsche, Ford and Lotus.

934
00:59:29,120 --> 00:59:30,350
重新上路，
Back on the move,

935
00:59:30,400 --> 00:59:33,390
他们现在朝大得多的里奥格兰德镇进发，
they were now heading for
the much larger town of Rio Grande,

936
00:59:33,440 --> 00:59:38,160
据说那儿有大约三百辆车的车队在等着他们。
where they were told a mob
in some 300 cars was waiting.

937
00:59:57,480 --> 01:00:00,470
害怕丢了小命，车队抛弃了道路
Fearing for their lives,
the crew abandoned the road

938
01:00:00,520 --> 01:00:04,800
向我们之前走过的河边跨国奔去。
and headed cross-country towards
the river border we'd used earlier.

939
01:00:20,600 --> 01:00:22,710
警车护送在后面跟着
With the police escort hanging back

940
01:00:22,760 --> 01:00:25,830
确保攻击者没发现我们的伎俩，
to make sure the attackers
hadn't spotted the ruse,

941
01:00:25,880 --> 01:00:29,630
车队终于到达河边，几小时后
the convoy made it to the river,
where a few hours later

942
01:00:29,680 --> 01:00:33,200
天光照亮了这场袭击的残忍。
daylight revealed the
viciousness of the attack.

943
01:00:53,440 --> 01:00:58,670
这回，连挖掘机和卡车都没有，过河只能靠自己。
This time, there were no diggers
or trucks to help ford the river.

944
01:00:58,720 --> 01:00:59,830
快点！
Come on!

945
01:00:59,880 --> 01:01:04,670
但经过数小时的挣扎，我们的队伍终于渡过去了……
But after many hours of struggle,
our team made it across...

946
01:01:04,720 --> 01:01:06,870
车子嗡嗡
CARS BEEP

947
01:01:06,920 --> 01:01:09,760
欢呼
CHEERING

948
01:01:12,240 --> 01:01:15,630
…进入了智利热情的怀抱。
.. and into the welcoming
arms of Chile.

949
01:01:15,680 --> 01:01:17,960
很高兴见到你们。
We are happy to see you.

950
01:01:27,480 --> 01:01:32,310
而我们三个人，则决定用
'Us three, meanwhile, had decided
to conclude this whole sorry saga in

951
01:01:32,360 --> 01:01:37,080
和巴奇·卡西迪、日光小子结束他们的方式一样结束这段可怜的 saga。
'the same way that Butch Cassidy and
the Sundance Kid had ended theirs.'

952
01:01:38,680 --> 01:01:40,350
我灵机一动。
I've had a great idea.

953
01:01:40,400 --> 01:01:43,110
~ 什么？ ~ 澳大利亚。 ~ 澳大利亚？
~ What? ~ Australia. ~ Australia?

954
01:01:43,160 --> 01:01:47,550
~ 对啊，他们有马，你可以学骑。 ~ 没有马！
~ Yeah, they've got horses, you could
learn to ride. ~ No horses!

955
01:01:47,600 --> 01:01:49,110
好了，听好了。
Well, listen.

956
01:01:49,160 --> 01:01:53,360
离开这里后记住一点……
The important thing to remember
when we get out of here is...

957
01:01:56,680 --> 01:02:00,910
~ 等一下，你看到那边的2CV了吗？ ~ 2CV？没有。
~ Hang on, did you see
the 2CV out there? ~ 2CV? No.

958
01:02:00,960 --> 01:02:04,200
哦，太好了，我刚才还以为我们有麻烦了。对吧。
Oh, good. For a moment then
I thought we were in trouble. Right.

959
01:02:07,080 --> 01:02:08,110
火啊！
Fuego!

960
01:02:08,160 --> 01:02:11,190
枪声
GUNFIRE

961
01:02:11,240 --> 01:02:12,350
开火！
Fuego!

962
01:02:12,400 --> 01:02:15,790
枪声！
GUNFIRE

963
01:02:15,840 --> 01:02:18,880
钢琴音乐：《不再回家》
